      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Playing Bloodstained Mire instead of Swamp wastes 1 life when cracking the fetch, and the player wants to cast Thoughtseize (costs B) or Faithless Looting (costs R) this turn. If they play Swamp, they can cast Thoughtseize immediately for free (no life from fetch). If they play Bloodstained Mire, they need to crack it (paying 1 life) to get a Swamp to cast Thoughtseize, losing 1 unnecessary life point. The fetch land should be saved for later when color flexibility is actually needed or when revolt for Fatal Push matters. Playing Swamp directly and saving the fetchland preserves life and keeps open the option to trigger revolt with Bloodstained Mire on a future turn when Fatal Push needs to hit a 3-4 mana value creature.",
      "action_taken": "Played Bloodstained Mire as the land drop for turn 1.",
