      "description": "Casting Quantum Riddler (via Warp for 1U) instead of Faithful Mending (WU) on turn 4 with 4 mana available. Faithful Mending would draw 2 cards, discard 2, gain 2 life, and help fill the graveyard to set up future plays like Abhorrent Oculus or fuel graveyard synergies. It also leaves mana open for potential interaction. The Quantum Riddler as a 2/2 face-down creature (Warp puts it face-down as a 2/2 manifest) only draws a card when it enters face-up. Actually, looking more carefully at Warp - Warp {1}{U} manifests the creature, putting it face down as a 2/2. It doesn't trigger the ETB draw. However, you can later pay its full mana cost to flip it face up and get the ETB trigger. The question is whether a 2/2 body now is better than Faithful Mending's card filtering and life gain. With the opponent at low pressure (only an Undercity Sewers tapped, no creatures), Faithful Mending to dig toward answers and set up the graveyard for later flashback seems reasonable. But a 2/2 body that can later flip into a 4/6 flyer with card draw is also fine. This is debatable but Faithful Mending at end of opponent's turn would have been more flexible, preserving the option to cast Riddler later while getting card selection now.",
