    {
      "severity": "major",
      "description": "Llama4 Johnny used Thoughtseize to take Ephemerate from Grok4F ESPN's hand, but the opponent's hand contains Goryo's Vengeance and TWO copies of Atraxa, Grand Unifier. Goryo's Vengeance is the most dangerous card here — it can instantly reanimate Atraxa (which is legendary) at instant speed, creating a 7/7 with flying, vigilance, deathtouch, lifelink that draws ~4-5 cards on ETB. The opponent already has a Psychic Frog in graveyard and could discard an Atraxa to set up Goryo's Vengeance. Ephemerate is relatively low-impact when the opponent has no creatures on board. Taking Goryo's Vengeance removes the explosive reanimation threat, while taking Ephemerate does almost nothing meaningful.",
      "action_taken": "Chose Ephemerate with Thoughtseize",
      "better_line": "Take Goryo's Vengeance with Thoughtseize to prevent the opponent from reanimating Atraxa, Grand Unifier. The opponent could easily discard an Atraxa to Faithful Mending and then use Goryo's Vengeance to put it into play, generating massive card advantage and a huge threat.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 62,
      "player": "Llama4 Johnny",
      "decision_index": 56,
