      "decision_index": 100,
    },
    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "Discarding Bitter Triumph removes the only removal spell in hand, while Archon of Cruelty is an 8-mana creature that is extremely unlikely to be hardcast with only 4 lands in play and no reanimation targets set up (no way to get it into the graveyard and reanimate it since Unearth can only target MV 3 or less, and there are no Goryo's Vengeance in hand). Bitter Triumph is a flexible instant-speed removal spell that could answer the opponent's Quantum Riddler or future threats. Discarding Archon of Cruelty instead would pump the Frog equally while keeping the removal spell, and the Archon in the graveyard could potentially be reanimated later if a Goryo's Vengeance is drawn (it's legendary, making it a valid target).",
      "action_taken": "Discarded Bitter Triumph to pump Psychic Frog, keeping Archon of Cruelty in hand.",
