      "decision_index": 117,
    },
    {
      "severity": "major",
      "description": "Evoked Solitude by exiling Atraxa, Grand Unifier from hand with no enemy creatures on the battlefield to exile. This wastes both Solitude and Atraxa (two cards) to accomplish nothing. The opponent has Thoughtseize on the stack which would only take one card. By evoking Solitude, they lose two cards instead of one.",
      "action_taken": "Chose to evoke Solitude, exiling Atraxa Grand Unifier as the white card cost, with no opposing creatures to target.",
      "better_line": "Let Thoughtseize resolve and lose one card (likely Atraxa or a Force of Negation), preserving the other cards. Alternatively, if they wanted to protect a specific card, use Force of Negation to counter Thoughtseize (exiling a blue card - Force of Negation - to counter the noncreature spell for free since it's not their turn... wait, it IS their turn). Since it's their turn, Force of Negation can't be cast for free. Simply letting Thoughtseize resolve and losing one card is far better than losing two cards for no effect.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 119,
      "player": "Grok4F ESPN",
      "decision_index": 119,
    },
    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "Grok4F ESPN chose to discard Archon of Cruelty with Thoughtseize, but Llama4 Johnny's graveyard is already stocked with reanimation-friendly cards and Johnny has no way to cheat Archon into play from hand with only 3 lands (2 untapped). The two Faithless Lootings are far more dangerous - they let Johnny dig for threats, fill the graveyard further, and find answers. With Faithless Looting, Johnny can draw into reanimation spells, more threats, or disruption while also fueling graveyard synergies. Archon of Cruelty costs 8 mana and Johnny is on 3 lands with no ramp visible - it's extremely unlikely to be hardcast anytime soon. Meanwhile, Faithless Looting (especially with flashback) provides consistent card selection and graveyard filling that enables Johnny's entire game plan. Taking a Faithless Looting would have been more impactful at slowing Johnny's development.",
      "action_taken": "Discarded Archon of Cruelty from opponent's hand with Thoughtseize",
