    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "Emperor of Bones exiles a card from a graveyard at the beginning of combat, and when it gets +1/+1 counters (via Adapt 2 for {1}{B}), it puts an exiled creature card onto the battlefield with haste. The player exiled Thoughtseize, a sorcery, which cannot be put onto the battlefield as a creature. The opponent's graveyard contains Atraxa, Grand Unifier and Solitude - extremely powerful creatures that could be reanimated with Emperor of Bones' adapt ability. Even from the player's own graveyard, Archon of Cruelty or Abhorrent Oculus would be high-impact targets. Exiling a sorcery wastes the Emperor's key ability entirely.",
